<title>HONG KONG: Great China posts lower year net profit.</title>
<headline>Great China posts lower year net profit.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended September 30</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   7.46	vs  19.04</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    1.6	 vs  0.6</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  1.90 gain vs  35.72 gain</p>
<p>    Net			    19.53     vs  49.82</p>
<p>    Turnover		     142.20    vs  91.88</p>
<p>    Company name		 Great China Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  January 13-20, 1997</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   March 7, 1997</p>
<p>NOTE - Great China is a holding company with interests in property, footwear manufacturing and garment distribution.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional gain on compensation received and surplus arising on liquidation of an associated company.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is 3.2 H.K. cents (including interim dividend of 1.6 cents) vs 2.2 cents.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
